From: NWA50BE OpenWrt Project <noreply@invalid.example>
Subject: [PATCH] dnsmasq: backport October 2026 security fixes
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only

Carry OpenWrt main 6db25ee835 onto dnsmasq 2.93 until 2.94 is out. The
seven upstream commits are added as patches 003 to 009 (dnsmasq commit
in brackets; upstream marks the CVE ids as "may apply"):

  003 zone_status() heap OOB read, CNVD-C-2026-590208 (f90df6c)
  004 find_soa() subdomain test, CVE-2026-93008 (7719737)
  005 DNSSEC TCP slot reserve, CVE-2026-93007 (11493fe)
  006 stale TFTP cache after free, CVE-2026-93006 (cdbfb97)
  007 DHCPv6 FQDN off-by-one, CVE-2026-93009 (a627a78)
  008 DNSSEC wildcard name overflow, CVE-2026-93011 (145abca)
  009 blockdata_read() heap OOB write, no CVE id yet (738c049)

The context in 100 and 200 is refreshed as in main. Main's 001 and 002
(SIGHUP reload speed-up) are not security fixes and are left out.
